# Edits to a migration that a release already shipped, accepted because they are safe for a site
# that ran the shipped version (a formatting change, or a fix that only matters where it failed).
#
# One edit per line: the blob the release shipped, the blob it is edited to, then the path.
#
#   git rev-parse <release tag>:database/migrations/<file>
#   git rev-parse HEAD:database/migrations/<file>
#
# A further edit to the same file needs a line of its own. A line stops matching once a release
# ships the edited file, and can be removed then.
